"""ant-facet-test-modules: donor-level facet tests of gene-module scores (v1, exploratory).

What it does
------------
Module-level sibling of ``ant-facet-test`` (which tests single genes). For
every eligible dataset (not in vitro, bulk, spatial or mass spectrometry; at
least 6 replicates; facet scopes of ``lib/facet_scopes.py``) and every cell
type stratum, tests the facets of the dataset's scope (sex, disease,
apoe4_carrier, braak, age and, in xenograft and mouse knock-in datasets,
app_nlgf; never the sensitivity facets such as age_adjusted) for every module
of every catalog present in the dataset's ``<stem>.scores.parquet`` sidecar.
Strata, donor tables, covariates, batch rules, minimum donors and the n_lt5
rule are the ones of the gene tool (they are literally its functions, imported
from ``ant-facet-test``). ``app_nlgf`` follows the gene tool exactly: the
``.md`` ``control_basis`` and ``app_nlgf_design`` (timepoint, graft line,
covariate columns) split a stratum into one unit per timepoint and graft line
(``celltype_source`` suffix ``@timepoint=6m|line=APOE33``, ``design_subset`` on
the rows and the unit record), and a unit confounded with a design covariate is
refused rather than tested.

Two variants, reported side by side (column ``method``):

  cell_mean    (A) per-cell module scores of the sidecar (scanpy score_genes
               on log-normalised X, source ``geneset``; ``--sources`` can add
               ``ucell``, the default tests both, each source is its own BH
               family) averaged per (donor, stratum). Needs no counts, so
               it also runs on datasets without a raw-counts layer (rows
               carry ``no_counts`` true).
  pseudobulk   (B) per (donor, stratum) raw counts are summed, converted to
               log2(CPM + 1), and the module score is the mean over the module
               genes minus the mean over an expression-matched control set
               (scanpy score_genes logic: 25 bins of the stratum's mean
               expression rank, 50 random controls per module gene, module
               genes excluded, seed recorded). Only for datasets with a served
               raw-counts layer and modules whose gene list is in the
               genesetstore (>= 3 genes found in the dataset).

Model per (dataset, stratum, facet, method): one OLS per module on the
donor-level scores, ``score ~ facet [+ sex] [+ age] [+ pmi] [+ batch]``
(design from ``plan_job`` of the gene tool), t test on the facet coefficient
(df = donors - parameters), 95 percent CI on the t quantile, and a
permutation p value from 10,000 shuffles of the facet labels across donors
(covariates fixed, t statistic of the full model as test statistic, the same
shuffles for every module of the unit and for both methods, seed derived from
the base seed and the unit key). Benjamini-Hochberg across the modules of one
(dataset, stratum, facet, method), separately for the parametric and the
permutation p values. Units with n_lt5 are descriptive only (estimates and SE
kept, p / q / t / CI NULL). A vs B effect-estimate correlation per unit is
written to the manifest (calibration check).

Cell type scope (2026-10-08): a module is tested only in strata whose cell
type group (``lib/celltype_groups.yaml``, ``group_of`` of the stratum label)
belongs to the group of the module's ``celltypes`` (geneset store; per-geneset
``.md`` override allowed); ``celltypes: [all]`` modules are tested in every
stratum and ``role: markers`` QC panels are never tested. The Benjamini-Hochberg
family of a (dataset, stratum, facet, method) is the set of modules in scope for
that stratum. The scores of a module exist only for the cells of its scope
(``ant-score-ext`` / ``ant-ucell``), so the donor means are taken over those cells.
There are no donor-pooled units in this tool, so the pooled (``--pool``) runs of
``ant-facet-test`` have no module counterpart.

Inputs: the h5adstore (read only: .md, .h5ad.mus, .duckdb, scores sidecar,
counts by_gene sidecar) and the genesetstore (module gene lists).
Outputs: only <h5adstore>/_facet_tests/<group>/<file>.facet_module_tests.parquet
and <file>.facet_module_run_manifest.json. Nothing else in data/ is written.

Usage::

  ant-facet-test-modules inventory [--out tsv]
  ant-facet-test-modules run --db-id G24/MMG [--facets braak,sex]
  ant-facet-test-modules run --all [--max-load 12]
  ant-facet-test-modules summarize --out-dir DIR
"""
